{
    "background_story": "Jayleen was a brilliant and ambitious architect who had always been fascinated by the concept of pavises, ancient shields used for protection. Growing up in a city plagued by natural disasters, she became determined to design buildings that could withstand the most extreme conditions. Jayleen spent years researching and experimenting, eventually developing a revolutionary new material that could absorb and distribute impact forces. Her innovative design, dubbed the 'Pavis System,' quickly gained international attention and acclaim. Governments and corporations clamored for her expertise, and Jayleen's firm became a leading authority on disaster-resistant construction. As she looked out over the city, she knew that her work would save countless lives and provide a safe haven for generations to come.",
